<div class="print-lifecycle container my-4">
  <h2>Statuses Overview</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>pending</strong> (0): New jobs start here; awaiting staff review, slicing, or clarification.</li>
    <li><strong>information_requested</strong> (1): Patron has received price/weight estimates and is awaiting their reply.</li>
    <li><strong>response_received</strong> (2): Patron responded to estimate; staff reviews for approval or cancellation.</li>
    <li><strong>approved</strong> (3): Patron approved estimate; job queued for printing.</li>
    <li><strong>in_progress</strong> (4): Job assigned to printer; printing underway.</li>
    <li><strong>ready_for_pickup</strong> (5): Print finished, post-processed, weighed, and patron notified.</li>
    <li><strong>archived</strong> (6): Patron picked up the print; job closed and archived.</li>
    <li><strong>ongoing</strong> (7): Staff-only filler prints to keep printers active.</li>
    <li><strong>cancelled</strong> (8): Patron declined estimate or staff cancelled the job.</li>
    <li><strong>rejected</strong> (9): Job rejected due to issues like unprintable models; not printed.</li>
    <li><strong>abandoned</strong> (10): Job abandoned by patron or staff; no further action.</li>
  </ul>
  <hr>

  <div class="accordion" id="lifecycleAccordion">

    <!-- 1. pending → information_requested -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-pending">
        <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-pending" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapse-pending">
          1. pending → information_requested
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-pending" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" aria-labelledby="heading-pending" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Patron submits a new print request (status set to <em>pending</em>).</li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Review model for scale, print type, and printability.</li>
                <li>Slice model to estimate filament weight and print time.</li>
                <li>Contact patron via conversation if clarification is needed.</li>
                <li>Record <em>slicer_weight</em> (Weight estimate).</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Automated:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Calculate <em>slicer_cost</em> (Estimated cost).</li>
                <li>Update status to <em>information_requested</em>.</li>
                <li>Send automated estimate message via JobMailer.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. information_requested → response_received -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-info">
        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-info" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-info">
          2. information_requested → response_received
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-info" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-info" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Patron replies to estimate message.</li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Review patron’s response.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Automated:</strong> Status changes to <em>response_received</em>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3. response_received → {approved / cancelled} -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-response">
        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-response" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-response">
          3. response_received → {approved / cancelled}
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-response" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-response" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Possible Outcomes:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li><em>approved</em>: Patron accepts estimate.</li>
                <li><em>cancelled</em>: Patron declines or staff cancels.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions (on approval):</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Update status to <em>approved</em>.</li>
                <li>Queue job for printing.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions (on cancellation):</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Update status to <em>cancelled</em>.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Automated:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Notify patron the job has been cancelled</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. approved → in_progress -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-approved">
        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-approved" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-approved">
          4. approved → in_progress
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-approved" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-approved" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Printer becomes available and staff starts the print.</li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Assign job to a printer.</li>
                <li>Update status to <em>in_progress</em>.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 5. in_progress → ready_for_pickup -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-progress">
        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-progress" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-progress">
          5. in_progress → ready_for_pickup
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-progress" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-progress" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Print run completes successfully.</li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Post-process (support removal, curing, cleaning).</li>
                <li>Weigh actual filament (or resin volume).</li>
                <li>Record actual weight.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Automated:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Update status to <em>ready_for_pickup</em>.</li>
                <li>Calculates cost based on entered weight.</li>
                <li>Notify patron via JobMailer that job is ready with actual cost.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 6. ready_for_pickup → archived -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-ready">
        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-ready" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-ready">
          6. ready_for_pickup → archived
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-ready" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-ready" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Patron picks up the finished print.</li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Enter Pickup Date.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Automated:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Job marked as <em>archived</em>.</li>
                <li>Optionally send feedback survey or follow-up message.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 7. ongoing (staff-only) -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-ongoing">
        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-ongoing" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-ongoing">
          7. ongoing (staff-only)
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-ongoing" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-ongoing" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Usage:</strong> Internal filler prints when no patron jobs are queued.</li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Staff manually assign or create <em>ongoing</em> jobs for assistive/fidget devices or programs.</li>
                <li>Increment Quantity for each printed object.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 8. cancelled -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-cancelled">
        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-cancelled" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-cancelled">
          8. cancelled
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-cancelled" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-cancelled" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Patron declines during <em>response_received</em> or staff cancels otherwise.</li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Update status to <em>cancelled</em>.</li>
                <li>Do not queue or print.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 9. rejected -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-rejected">
        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-rejected" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-rejected">
          9. rejected
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-rejected" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-rejected" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Staff rejects the job after review (e.g., unprintable model or violates policy).</li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Update status to <em>rejected</em>.</li>
                <li>Do not queue for printing.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Automated:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Notify the patron the job has been rejected.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 10. abandoned -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-abandoned">
        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-abandoned" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-abandoned">
          10. abandoned
        </button>
      </h2>
      <div id="collapse-abandoned" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-abandoned" data-bs-parent="#lifecycleAccordion">
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> Job abandoned by patron (not picked up within 30 days of completion).</li>
            <li><strong>Staff Actions:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Update status to <em>abandoned</em>.</li>
                <li>Dispose of print appropriately.</li>
                <li>Bill patron Evergreen account for cost of item (if they have an Evergreen account).</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="card mb-4 mt-4">
    <div class="card-header bg-light">
      <h3 class="mb-0">Automations</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <ul>
        <li>When entering <code>slicer_weight</code> (Weight estimate) and saving a job, the patron will be notified and status changed to <code>information_requested</code>.</li>
        <li>When a job is <code>information_requested</code> and the patron replies (email or web), the status automatically changes to <code>response_received</code>.</li>
        <li>When a job is <code>cancelled</code>, send a message notifying the patron (and consider allowing resubmission).</li>
        <li>Assigning a printer automatically sets the job’s <code>print_type</code>.</li>
        <li>Setting <code>actual_weight</code> (Weight) calculates cost, changes status to <code>ready_for_pickup</code>, and notifies patron.</li>
        <li>Entering pickup date changes status to <code>archived</code>.</li>
        <li>Setting job status to <code>cancelled</code> or <code>rejected</code> will notify the patron automatically.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card mb-4">
    <div class="card-header bg-light">
      <h3 class="mb-0">Additional Links</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <div><a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/e/2PACX-1vTGbtzPoaN7KHrZ9TnQZ2i-pXsRGGk_GuxUnFAbSKtQt6qKdpnCkvcAKpt6dskEe79w_H_sd2evAPot/pub" target="_blank">MAKEatTADL Staff Guide</a> (opens in a new tab)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
